type(scope): short subject, imperative, max 50 chars

Body — what and why, wrap at 72 chars. Explain the problem,
the solution, and any alternatives considered.

Footer: Fixes #123, Refs #456, BREAKING CHANGE: description

# Guidance (removed from commit — do not uncomment):
#  type: feat, fix, docs, style, refactor, perf, test, build, ci, chore, revert
#  scope: optional area, e.g. api, ui, auth, docs, deps
#  subject: imperative, lowercase, no trailing period, e.g. feat(auth): add password reset
#  body: explain what and why, not how; leave blank line above/below; wrap at 72 chars
#  footer: e.g. Fixes #123, Refs #456, BREAKING CHANGE: describe breakage
#  Keep commits focused; separate unrelated changes.
#  Never commit secrets or credentials; check staged files before committing.
